{"d":19,"passage":{"title":"白鲸","author":"Herman Melville","text":"Yes; these laws might be engraven on a Queen Anne's farthing, or the barb of a harpoon, and worn round the neck, so small are they. But what plays the mischief with this masterly code is the admirable brevity of it, which necessitates a vast volume of commentaries to expound it. These are scientific commentaries; but the commentaries of the whalemen themselves sometimes consist in hard words and harder knocks—the Coke-upon-Littleton of the fist. Ultimately the defendants (the crew of another ship) came up with the whale, struck, killed, seized, and finally appropriated it before the very eyes of the plaintiffs. Wherefore the plaintiffs now sued for the recovery of the value of their whale, line, harpoons, and boat. In the course of the defence, the witty Erskine went on to illustrate his position, by alluding to a recent crim. Now in the present case Erskine contended that the examples of the whale and the lady were reciprocally illustrative of each other."},"words":[{"w":"judges","uk":"'dʒʌdʒiz","us":"/'dʒʌdʒiz/","p":"","m":"n. 士师记（又译《民长记》, 旧约全书之一卷）","f":[],"c":["competent judges","best judges","judges right"],"o":{"t":"You cannot, at least, deny that you are very harsh judges of each other.","w":"基督山伯爵"},"q":{"t":"When he quitted me, he bade me be of good courage, and to rely upon his doing all in his power to convince my judges of my innocence.","w":"基督山伯爵","a":"Alexandre Dumas"},"b":{"r":"Exodus 22:8","c":"出埃及记 22:8","t":"If the thief be not found, then the master of the house shall be brought unto the judges, to see whether he have put his hand unto his neighbour’s goods."}},{"w":"migrate","uk":"/maɪˈɡreɪt/","us":"/maɪˈɡreɪt/","p":"v.","m":"迁徙；移居","f":["migrating","immigrate"],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"The answer, as I believe, is, that mammals have not been able to migrate, whereas some plants, from their varied means of dispersal, have migrated across the vast and broken interspace.","w":"物种起源","a":"Charles Darwin"},"b":null},{"w":"consist","uk":"kən'sist","us":"/kən'sist/","p":"","m":"vi. 组成, 存在于, 一致","f":["consistent","consistence","consisting"],"c":["consisted almost","party consisted","consist altogether"],"o":{"t":"But Peppino did not even belong to my band; he was merely a poor shepherd, whose only crime consisted in furnishing us with provisions.","w":"基督山伯爵"},"q":{"t":"The whole furniture consisted of a chair, a clothes-press, and a large oak case, with squares cut out near the top resembling coach windows.","w":"呼啸山庄","a":"Emily Bronte"},"b":{"r":"Colossians 1:17","c":"歌罗西书 1:17","t":"And he is before all things, and by him all things consist."}},{"w":"zealand","uk":"'ziːlənd","us":"/'ziːlənd/","p":"","m":"n. 西兰岛（丹麦最大的岛）","f":[],"c":["new zealand"],"o":null,"q":{"t":"Sir J. Richardson, also, speaks of the reappearance on the shores of New Zealand, Tasmania, etc., of northern forms of fish.","w":"物种起源","a":"Charles Darwin"},"b":null},{"w":"examples","uk":"","us":"","p":"","m":"n. 例子；列证（example的复数形式）","f":[],"c":["many examples"],"o":null,"q":{"t":"I might proceed with several more examples, one way or another known to me, of the great power and malice at times of the sperm whale.","w":"白鲸","a":"Herman Melville"},"b":{"r":"1 Corinthians 10:6","c":"哥林多前书 10:6","t":"Now these things were our examples, to the intent we should not lust after evil things, as they also lusted."}},{"w":"fort","uk":"fɒːt","us":"/fɑt/","p":"","m":"n. 堡垒, 要塞, 易货站 vt. 设要塞保卫 vi. 设要塞","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"For the second of these purposes, the maintenance of the forts and garrisons, an annual sum has been allotted to them by parliament, generally about £13,000.","w":"国富论","a":"Adam Smith"},"b":{"r":"Isaiah 29:3","c":"以赛亚书 29:3","t":"And I will camp against thee round about, and will lay siege against thee with a mount, and I will raise forts against thee."}},{"w":"certificates","uk":"səˈtifikeits","us":"/səˈtifikeits/","p":"","m":"n. 证明书, 执照( certificate的名词复数 )","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"In order to restore, in some measure, that free circulation of labour which those different statutes had almost entirely taken away, the invention of certificates was fallen upon.","w":"国富论","a":"Adam Smith"},"b":null},{"w":"sweden","uk":"'swiːdn","us":"/'swiːdn/","p":"","m":"n. 瑞典","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"But being neglected by Sweden, it was soon swallowed up by the Dutch colony of New York, which again, in 1674, fell under the dominion of the English.","w":"国富论","a":"Adam Smith"},"b":null},{"w":"checks","uk":"","us":"","p":"","m":"n. 支票；格（check的复数形式）","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"Possibly the checks they had devised for the increase of population had succeeded too well, and their numbers had rather diminished than kept stationary.","w":"世界大战","a":"H. G. Wells"},"b":null},{"w":"antonio","uk":"æn'təuniəu","us":"/æn'təuniəu/","p":"","m":"n. 安东尼奥（男名）","f":[],"c":["messer antonio"],"o":null,"q":{"t":"To this family was born a son Antonio, who became a priest of the order of San Michele of Lucca, and for this reason was honoured with the title of Messer Antonio.","w":"君主论","a":"Niccolo Machiavelli"},"b":null},{"w":"represents","uk":"ˌrepriˈzents","us":"/ˌrepriˈzents/","p":"","m":"v. 表现( represent的第三人称单数 ); 代表; 体现; 作为…的代表","f":[],"c":[],"o":{"t":"Come, your jealousy represents everything to you in the wrong light.","w":"基督山伯爵"},"q":{"t":"The first harmony of 400, as has been already remarked, probably represents the rulers; the second and oblong harmony of 7600, the people.","w":"理想国","a":"Plato (B. Jowett trans.)"},"b":null},{"w":"denmark","uk":"'denmɑːk","us":"/'denmɑk/","p":"","m":"n. 丹麦","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"On our arrival in Denmark, we found the king and queen of that country elevated in two arm-chairs on a kitchen-table, holding a Court.","w":"远大前程","a":"Charles Dickens"},"b":null},{"w":"improvements","uk":"ɪmp'ruːvmənts","us":"/ɪmp'ruːvmənts/","p":"","m":"n. 增加或修改( improvement的复数形式 ); 改进; 改善; 改良","f":[],"c":["greatest improvements","important improvements","improvements besides"],"o":null,"q":{"t":"Mrs. Norris, who had begun to redden, was appeased; and, for a little while, other subjects took place of the improvements of Sotherton.","w":"曼斯菲尔德庄园","a":"Jane Austen"},"b":null},{"w":"elections","uk":"","us":"","p":"","m":"n. 选举, 选举制；投票（election的复数形式）","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"The citizens, therefore, who had no land, had scarce any other means of subsistence but the bounties of the candidates at the annual elections.","w":"国富论","a":"Adam Smith"},"b":null},{"w":"causes","uk":"","us":"","p":"","m":"n. 原因","f":[],"c":["principal causes","different causes","several causes"],"o":null,"q":{"t":"The slightest provocation, even being asked if there is anything he would prefer for dinner, causes him to express a wish for a separation.","w":"月亮宝石","a":"Wilkie Collins"},"b":{"r":"Exodus 18:26","c":"出埃及记 18:26","t":"And they judged the people at all seasons: the hard causes they brought unto Moses, but every small matter they judged themselves."}},{"w":"hybridisation","uk":"/ˌhaɪbrɪdaɪˈzeɪʃən/","us":"/ˌhaɪbrɪdaɪˈzeɪʃən/","p":"n.","m":"杂交(= hybridization)","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"The following rules and conclusions are chiefly drawn up from Gärtner's admirable work on the hybridisation of plants.","w":"物种起源","a":"Charles Darwin"},"b":null},{"w":"arable","uk":"/ˈærəb(ə)l/","us":"/ˈærəb(ə)l/","p":"adj.","m":"适于耕种的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"In the Venetian territory, all the arable lands which are given in lease to farmers are taxed at a tenth of the rent.","w":"国富论","a":"Adam Smith"},"b":null},{"w":"inductive","uk":"/ɪnˈdʌktɪv/","us":"/ɪnˈdʌktɪv/","p":"adj.","m":"归纳的；诱导的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"Anticipations or divinations, or prophetic glimpses of truths whether concerning man or nature, seem to stand in the same relation to ancient philosophy which hypotheses bear to modern inductive science.","w":"理想国","a":"Plato (B. Jowett trans.)"},"b":null},{"w":"specialise","uk":"/ˈspeʃəlaɪz/","us":"/ˈspeʃəlaɪz/","p":"v.","m":"(= specialize)v. 专攻","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"It is probably from this same cause that organic beings low in the scale of nature are more variable than those which have their whole organisation more specialised, and are higher in the scale.","w":"物种起源","a":"Charles Darwin"},"b":null},{"w":"counterfeit","uk":"/ˈkaʊntəfɪt/","us":"/ˈkaʊntəfɪt/","p":"adj.","m":"假冒的 v. 伪造","f":[],"c":[],"o":{"t":"I scorn the counterfeit sentiment you offer: yes, St. John, and I scorn you when you offer it.","w":"简·爱"},"q":{"t":"Such is his distrust in the justice of his assessors, that he counterfeits poverty, and wishes to appear scarce able to pay anything, for fear of being obliged to pay too much.","w":"国富论","a":"Adam Smith"},"b":null},{"w":"legislate","uk":"/ˈledʒɪsleɪt/","us":"/ˈledʒɪsleɪt/","p":"v.","m":"立法，制定(或通过)法律","f":["legislative","legislature","legislator"],"c":["legislate whenever"],"o":{"t":"I claim, as a citizen, a right to legislate whenever my social rights are invaded by the social act of another.","w":"论自由"},"q":{"t":"But there is, I think, small wisdom in legislating about such matters,—I doubt if it is ever done; nor are any precise written enactments about them likely to be lasting.","w":"理想国","a":"Plato (B. Jowett trans.)"},"b":null},{"w":"oxide","uk":"/ˈɒksaɪd/","us":"/ˈɑksaɪd/","p":"n.","m":"氧化物","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"tsunami","uk":"/tsuːˈnɑːmi/","us":"/tsuːˈnɑmi/","p":"n.","m":"海啸","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"terrain","uk":"/təˈreɪn/","us":"/təˈreɪn/","p":"n.","m":"地形","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"thermal","uk":"/ˈθɜːm(ə)l/","us":"/ˈθɜrm(ə)l/","p":"adj.","m":"热量的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"toxic","uk":"/ˈtɒksɪk/","us":"/ˈtɑksɪk/","p":"adj.","m":"有毒的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"intensive","uk":"/ɪnˈtensɪv/","us":"/ɪnˈtensɪv/","p":"adj.","m":"加强的，集中的，密集的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q"